  "scope": {
    "test": "Literal spectralTest ell Y, Y>0 and original period 64; rapid bound constant may depend on ell,Y. For real t, H=8 cosh(pi*t) times the K_{2it} transform. For each real alpha in [0,1/2], raw 8 K_{2alpha} transform bounded uniformly in alpha and absolutely integrable in its defining q variable.",
    "coefficients": "Full marked M/N original functions for any actual positive level, with both original observation cusps and all singular incoming cusps, regular and exceptional actual basis labels, 1/(4pi cosh(pi t)) kept exactly once. Absolute convergence uses the fixed-level mass theorem and restored measurability of the complex covariance.",
    "caller": "Every nonzero original joint beta and occupied p supplies an occupied k,z,n with one strictly positive and one strictly negative Poisson-normalized second index, both with nonzero product W*traceBeta. The original arithmetic singleton fixes s=1 and leaves both Poisson signs.",
    "assembly": "Use T21 original_prescribed_opposite_trace on each true chart row, reindex Nat+ to natural c with zero term excluded, recover fullModulusRow and fullChartMode with original M sqrt(fixedZ), both charts and period-64 coefficient. For every original key and Poisson block the negative trace is replaced, positive fullBlockMode retained. Six scale pairs, one global cutoff, explicit zero-y/zero-m/tail remainder, actual outer HasSum; no exchange of Fourier marking ell and inner infinite spectra."
  },
  "unpaid": [
    "Prescribed positive-sign Maass/continuous J trace and summed even-weight holomorphic contribution in the normalized infinity and one frames, with the same original marking. The per-form coefficient and slash identities are already available.",
    "Quantitative regular cumulative large sieve and exceptional A/J estimates with original level/frequency costs, true oldform removal, all-cost 7/32.",
    "Same-source kernel verification and inherited provider staging."
  ],
